Part VII — Attack our entire prior research

Once all engine research is complete, assume the whole research program is wrong.

Conduct a dedicated adversarial reconciliation.

Try to prove:

llama.cpp should be replaced;

llama.cpp should definitely not be replaced;

Vulkan is worse than CPU for common Prism workloads;

OpenCL is not worth maintaining;

OpenCL is actually the best Snapdragon route;

NPU integration is premature;

NPU integration should be moved earlier;

speculative decoding is worthless on a phone;

speculative decoding is one of the biggest available wins;

larger context hurts more than it helps;

KV quantization meaningfully damages quality;

our memory estimates are dangerously optimistic;

our GPU-offload assumptions are incorrect;

our benchmark suite measures the wrong things;

our custom context manipulation creates correctness risk;

Android thermal limits dominate all kernel-level optimization.

Where competing hypotheses remain unresolved, specify the experiment that resolves them.

Do not manufacture certainty.

