Research standards

Prefer:

source code;

official repository documentation;

official technical docs;

GitHub issues/PRs;

reproducible benchmarks;

independent benchmarks;

vendor claims last.

For any important performance claim identify its evidence quality.

Do not cite SEO summaries when primary sources are available.

Do not copy benchmark numbers without understanding their conditions.

Use exact dates and versions where relevant.

Engineering rules

Do not propose a giant rewrite unless the evidence clearly demands one.

Do not sacrifice arbitrary GGUF compatibility casually.

Do not create backend abstractions for hypothetical future systems unless they solve a concrete current problem.

Do not assume GPU > CPU.

Do not assume NPU > GPU.

Do not assume more GPU layers are always faster.

Do not assume more threads are faster.

Do not assume longer context is better.

Do not assume Q4 KV is safe for every model.

Do not assume vendor benchmark claims generalize to Prism.

Do not confuse:

PP tok/s;

TG tok/s;

TTFT;

sustained throughput.

Treat them as separate objectives.

Do not optimize benchmark numbers at the expense of actual chat performance.

Central principle

The desired end-state is not:

«"Prism has lots of inference settings."»

The desired end-state is:

«Prism understands the device, understands the model, understands its measured history, selects a defensible execution plan automatically, observes whether that plan actually worked, and learns a better configuration without sacrificing correctness or reliability.»

The user should generally not need to understand:

GPU layers;

microbatch sizes;

CPU affinity;

KV cache formats;

backend quirks.

Expert controls may remain available, but the default system should make the decision.

Final question you must answer

After completing all research and adversarial analysis, make a concrete recommendation:

«What exact sequence of engineering work gives PrismLocal the greatest probability of becoming materially faster, more memory-efficient, more thermally sustainable, more reliable, and more capable than its present implementation without burying the project under unnecessary runtime complexity?»

The answer must be expressed as an evidence-backed roadmap and executable agent program, not merely prose recommendations.
